# The harness's `screendump:` end to end on OVMF's own screen, which no
# host model draws, so `--bless` writes its golden, unlike the tui
# scenario's (docs/design.md, "The harness"): QMP's screendump, QEMU's
# PPM, the PNG and the exact comparison with tests/qemu/golden/ovmf.png.
# The release kernel boots `test=release`, whose root task waits for a
# line, so the screen holds still while it is taken: q35's std VGA at the
# 1280x800 OVMF picks from its EDID, showing what OVMF left there,
# TianoCore's logo and its two BdsDxe lines, since nothing after the
# firmware draws in this test (the loader writes only COM1, and
# test=release starts no term). OVMF's text is drawn as its lines reach COM1,
# so a screendump taken before the loader starts can catch it part drawn;
# this one comes long after. The rest is release.scenario's run, shortened.
kernel: release
cmdline: test=release
exit: success
expect: loader: GOP framebuffer 1280x800
expect: entering kernel
expect: release: type a line
screendump: ovmf
send: release input\r          # the line root checks for
expect: release: read "release input"
expect: TEST PASS
